L0110: Proof type marker used as a proof block

The @ marker introduces a proof type or separates a proposition constructor from its evidence. It is not an expression block opener. Use prove!(claim), a named proof value, or an ordinary block that returns evidence.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/proof_block.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
// `@` begins a proof type and nothing else: `@{ _ }` is not an expression.
fn first(n: u8) -> (out: u8, @(out == n)) {
    (n, @{ _ })
}
```

Language, as built: [1.7:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.7:1).
